{"id":9154,"date":"2020-06-23T00:00:00","date_gmt":"2020-06-23T06:00:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.rethinkfirst.com\/resources\/teaching-learners-with-autism-to-cooperate-with-wearing-masks-video\/"},"modified":"2025-02-27T17:54:53","modified_gmt":"2025-02-27T22:54:53","slug":"teaching-learners-with-autism-to-cooperate-with-wearing-masks-video","status":"publish","type":"resources","link":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/resources\/teaching-learners-with-autism-to-cooperate-with-wearing-masks-video\/","title":{"rendered":"Teaching Learners with Autism to Cooperate with Wearing Masks"},"content":{"rendered":"\t\t<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"9154\" class=\"elementor elementor-9154\" data-elementor-post-type=\"resources\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<section class=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-5d404ac9 elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default\" data-id=\"5d404ac9\" data-element_type=\"section\" data-settings=\"{&quot;jet_parallax_layout_list&quot;:[]}\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-100 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-4ddaf457\" data-id=\"4ddaf457\" data-element_type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-7591c28c elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"7591c28c\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"videoDivHolder\"><div><video poster=\"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/10\/485-MzA0NDQ1_teaching-learners-autism-to-cooperate-wearing-masks_thumbnail.jpg\" controls=\"controls\" width=\"300\" height=\"150\"> <source src=\"https:\/\/rtaprodmarketing.blob.core.windows.net\/rta-prod-marketingvideos\/485-MzA0NDQ1_teaching-learners-autism-to-cooperate-wearing-masks.mp4\" type=\"video\/mp4\" \/> <\/video><\/div><\/div><p><style> #videoDivHolder { width: 100%; max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; } #videoDivHolder > div { position: relative; overflow: hidden; width: 100%; padding-top: 56.25%; } #videoDivHolder > div video { position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; bottom: 0; right: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; } <\/style><\/p><h2>About this Webinar<\/h2><p>Given many states, local, and business mandates during the current pandemic, it is likely that students and clients will <a href=\"https:\/\/www.cdc.gov\/coronavirus\/2019-ncov\/prevent-getting-sick\/about-face-coverings.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">continue to be required to wear facial masks<\/a> when attending school, work, and other community activities for the foreseeable future.<\/p><p>Compliance with wearing a face mask can be challenging for individuals with autism and other developmental disabilities. Often staff may see an increase in behavioral challenges related to clients tolerating masks worn by others, putting on a mask themselves, or adhering to long durations of mask-wearing. With these challenges may often come a correlated decrease in on-task behaviors related to learning or work responsibilities.<\/p><p>While increasing learner cooperation with wearing masks may be a novel skill being targeted by clinicians with their clients, the strategies for doing so are not. Although research is still limited on gaining compliance with masks, previous research can be extended to successfully target this particular skill. Behavior analytic programming has been shown effective in teaching skills such as tolerating hair cuts, blood draws, toothbrushing, and visits to doctors\u2019 offices, as well as compliance with wearing eyeglasses and medical alert bracelets. These technologies can be extrapolated and utilized to also increase toleration and cooperation with wearing masks.<\/p><p><em>If you enjoyed this webinar, we recommend checking out our <a href=\"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/resources\/aba-telehealth-webinar-how-to-support-families-remotely\/\">ABA Telehealth Webinar: How To Support Families Remotely<\/a> webinar<\/em>.<\/p><h2>About the Guest Speaker<\/h2>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-520ea2b authorSection elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default\" data-id=\"520ea2b\" data-element_type=\"section\" data-settings=\"{&quot;jet_parallax_layout_list&quot;:[]}\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-33 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-ff794d2\" data-id=\"ff794d2\" data-element_type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-d0eedaf elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\" data-id=\"d0eedaf\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"image.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"600\" height=\"600\" src=\"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/06\/erin-richard-white-phd-bcba-d.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full wp-image-20850\" alt=\"Erin Richard White, Ph.D., BCBA-D\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/06\/erin-richard-white-phd-bcba-d.jpg 600w, https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/06\/erin-richard-white-phd-bcba-d-300x300.jpg 300w, https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/06\/erin-richard-white-phd-bcba-d-150x150.jpg 150w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px\" \/>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-66 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-d3ae91f\" data-id=\"d3ae91f\" data-element_type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-ed40a5c elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"ed40a5c\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h3>Erin Richard White, Ph.D., BCBA-D<\/h3><p style=\"font-size: var( --e-global-typography-159609b-font-size);\"><span style=\"color: #333333;\">BCBA at<\/span> <a href=\"https:\/\/www.atlantichealth.org\/about-us\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Atlantic Health System<\/a><\/p><p>Dr. Erin Richard White of Atlantic Health System (previously <a href=\"https:\/\/www.alpinelearninggroup.org\/about-alpine-learning-group\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Alpine Learning Group<\/a>) presents several teaching options that can be effective with a variety of learners, including providing choice, using desensitization and shaping techniques, programming reinforcement, modeling, and other antecedent and consequence strategies.<\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t","protected":false},"author":19,"featured_media":15021,"template":"","meta":{"_seopress_robots_primary_cat":"","_seopress_titles_title":"Webinar: Teaching Autism Learners to Cooperate Wearing Masks","_seopress_titles_desc":"Several teaching options that can be effective with a variety of learners, including providing choice, using desensitization and shaping techniques, and more.","_seopress_robots_index":"","om_disable_all_campaigns":